,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Who selects:** Under Section 32(a) of the Investment Company Act of 1940, the trust's board selects the independent public accountant. The vote requires a majority of the board, including a majority of the independent (non-\"interested\") trustees. It must occur within 30 days before or after the start of the fiscal year, or before the annual shareholder meeting. For exchange-listed ETFs, Exchange Act Rule 10A-3 and the listing standards also require an independent audit committee that directly appoints and oversees the auditor.\n\n**When ratification can be omitted:**\n1. **No annual meeting.** Section 32(a) requires ratification only at the next annual meeting \"if such meeting is held.\" Most Delaware and Massachusetts trusts don't hold annual meetings, so the issue rarely arises.\n2. **Rule 32a-4 exemption.** Ratification is not required if the fund has:\n   - an audit committee made up entirely of independent trustees,\n   - a board-adopted committee charter, and\n   - committee oversight of the auditor, with the charter kept as a record.\n\nSelection and termination still rest with the board and committee.","ttft_ms":4400,"type":"result","duration_ms":7966,"uuid":"153e6a77-4040-4de2-94e7-b9f00b1b0f76","ttft_stream_ms":540,"time_to_request_ms":65,"first_content_frame_ms":540,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
